From b0f8e8dc8d3ce39c82358e29e320cca4112b172e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMB-1 FM6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:44:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] 1.4.3 .. 1.4.7: Off targets, the covers, scopes and a live
 score, the dice on every knob, built-in DX7 banks, overload shedding, the
 review's fixes

- Off, every modulator's first target and its default (the voices' and the reel's); format 14 (13's targets one on,
  one at depth 0 Off)
- each page an album's colours and look (the covers drawn anew), scanlines, registration marks, a glitch at each new
  chord, a terminal cursor, Setup's live hex dump; the reel's spools as Volume II's circles
- each voice's page an oscilloscope of its own sound (Y-T, X-Y, polar); the first page (Partiture) and Space and
  Setup a live grand-staff score of the notes played (the engine keeps the last 48)
- SEL's dice roll every knob of every page (OP 2..5, LFO 2, Pitch EG, all six operators, all five modulators);
  a check that none is left unmoved
- the 16 DX7 banks built in (bank_rom.h, tools/gen_banks.py): a bank never sent plays the built-in one
- the meters: each voice's own level and the mix (M), in dB; long patch names fitted
- an overload (APP_OVERLOAD, lasting two renders) sheds a reel gene, else the softest bell, instead of the audio
  looping; Setup shows the xruns
- fixes: EDIT while overdubbing finishes the block (no noise), the reel's "full" as the engine has it, no erase while
  the reel saves, the score's notes closed on stop and role change, the Setup header never overlaps, All notes off
  only with MIDI out on
- tools/make_installer.py: the installer as one page (the firmware and M-VAVE's V15 inside), Portuguese first

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
